Bundled binaries
----------------
Every installer ships `resources/omp` (macOS arm64), `resources/omp.x64`
(macOS Intel), `resources/omp.exe` (Windows x64) or the Linux equivalent: a
compiled oh-my-pi agent built from the exact fork commit recorded in
`sidecar-source.json`. The fork carries WISA changes and retains the agent's
MIT license and notices. These binaries are build artifacts produced by
`bun run build:omp*`, not committed to this repository.

What WISA adds
--------------
- Product name, window titles, tray labels, installer artifact names.
- Vietnamese localization of the interface (upstream ships English, Chinese,
  Russian and Thai).
- A pre-seeded `wisa` provider pointing at https://api.askwisa.com/v1, so one
  WISA API key reaches every model the gateway serves. Any other provider the
  upstream agent supports still works.
- Release metadata pointing at this repository.

Bundled and downloaded components
---------------------------------
Piper (https://github.com/rhasspy/piper, MIT) and its Vietnamese voice model
vi_VN-vais1000-medium are downloaded on first use, not shipped in the
installer. The exact upstream revision and SHA-256 checksums are pinned in
src/main/piper.ts. Its model card documents fine-tuning from Lessac and uses
Truong Do's Northern Vietnamese VAIS-1000 corpus, CC BY 4.0:
https://doi.org/10.21227/H2B887
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
https://huggingface.co/rhasspy/piper-voices/blob/217ddc79818708b078d0d14a8fae9608b9d77141/vi/vi_VN/vais1000/medium/MODEL_CARD

Browser Use (https://github.com/browser-use/browser-use, MIT) ships as the
unmodified upstream Python distribution. The package's license is in its
wheel metadata. The local browser is Chromium from the official snapshots
archive, not Google Chrome. Its BSD license is at `browser-use/chromium/LICENSE`
in the app resources; Chromium lists third-party notices at `chrome://credits`.

